                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5fdf5013-8c3d-3672-be8d-967fb9ebb25f",
                        "entry_id": "295fcf2a-9b2f-3fda-9cda-57d16bbaa010",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui tient du poisson; relatif au poisson."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fea87a89-9158-49e6-83df-1e4c6f73f5cc",
                                "sense_id": "5fdf5013-8c3d-3672-be8d-967fb9ebb25f",
                                "text": "Miniature poissonnesque,\n Les vérons, topazes des eaux,\n Brillent : ceux-ci mignons fuseaux,\n Et ceux-là filiformes presque."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b280f6c-5826-4320-8740-9c1c7ac5b7c4",
                                "sense_id": "5fdf5013-8c3d-3672-be8d-967fb9ebb25f",
                                "text": "L’océan fera bon accueil à tout ce qui est d’origine poissonnesque."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68917f21-6a64-4d37-8c2a-4c46be676a22",
                                "sense_id": "5fdf5013-8c3d-3672-be8d-967fb9ebb25f",
                                "text": "La gent poissonnesque n’a pas fini de nous surprendre dans son continuel spectacle d’une vie effervescente."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "23c76323-2f5b-479e-85ca-e69d96149d71",
                        "source_entry_id": "295fcf2a-9b2f-3fda-9cda-57d16bbaa010",
                        "source_sense_id": "5fdf5013-8c3d-3672-be8d-967fb9ebb25f",
                        "target_lang_word": "fishlike",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fishlike",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "241eb83d-24bc-3983-ae6e-898829c54a5f",
                                        "entry_id": "ba3eee7a-0ce1-3291-9224-1b95516e6f6c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having some characteristics of a fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c09c7262-4980-4edb-ad38-cc8b1f4080da",
                                                "sense_id": "241eb83d-24bc-3983-ae6e-898829c54a5f",
                                                "text": "fishlike scales"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a456d59d-27b1-4df6-87c8-7d891e7d9725",
                                                "sense_id": "241eb83d-24bc-3983-ae6e-898829c54a5f",
                                                "text": "fishlike eyes"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "042c7c61-05e0-4b8d-91a0-c6001ee5b792",
                                                "sense_id": "241eb83d-24bc-3983-ae6e-898829c54a5f",
                                                "text": "fishlike swimming ability"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "857cf46e-8bf9-44f9-a31f-1b66a371f0a6",
                                                "sense_id": "241eb83d-24bc-3983-ae6e-898829c54a5f",
                                                "text": "fishlike smell"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10e84205-94bd-40c5-a8f7-ec569d3d80b0",
                                                "sense_id": "241eb83d-24bc-3983-ae6e-898829c54a5f",
                                                "text": "His skin was as scaly as those of some fish I'd seen. His nose was distorted—flattened from having been broken several times—and that enhanced his fishlike appearance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee2ebe3c-6d06-46df-913a-3d8c59cde017",
                                                "sense_id": "241eb83d-24bc-3983-ae6e-898829c54a5f",
                                                "text": "The most striking marine reptiles are the fishlike or porpoiselike ichthyosaurs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6ac1dd24-1938-445d-b01b-60dd2245aa0b",
                        "source_entry_id": "295fcf2a-9b2f-3fda-9cda-57d16bbaa010",
                        "source_sense_id": "5fdf5013-8c3d-3672-be8d-967fb9ebb25f",
                        "target_lang_word": "fishly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fishly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48f6e5b2-c410-3f8b-965e-c18155c5b89e",
                                        "entry_id": "a86de871-e808-3890-a671-883f0a284fdc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, relating to, characteristic of, or pertaining to fishes; piscine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "616ec47f-ee36-4ebc-a4b3-a77207543462",
                                                "sense_id": "48f6e5b2-c410-3f8b-965e-c18155c5b89e",
                                                "text": "[…] which fowles \"would strike at our men as they were aloft: \"some of them wee killed and eat: they seemed-\" to us very good, only tasted somewhat fishly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe413a80-b17f-4bcc-9f09-d4f25a7104f7",
                                                "sense_id": "48f6e5b2-c410-3f8b-965e-c18155c5b89e",
                                                "text": "Twice the cork bobbed prophecies of a fishly investigation. Twice the angler raised the squirming bait; but each time minus the scaly victim."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2fc0cea-03c5-4882-a5d1-6144684d909f",
                                                "sense_id": "48f6e5b2-c410-3f8b-965e-c18155c5b89e",
                                                "text": "At this the Fish did titter a fishly Titter, and Bit!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8511d8a1-26fb-49e1-8fa5-40bfe9fcb4e7",
                                                "sense_id": "48f6e5b2-c410-3f8b-965e-c18155c5b89e",
                                                "text": "It is a personality of a fishly sort."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fa9867d-527b-428a-ac61-5386e33509f2",
                                                "sense_id": "48f6e5b2-c410-3f8b-965e-c18155c5b89e",
                                                "text": "The perch, for example, regards the danger as exaggerated: all one needed was to exercise moderation, \"as a fishly virtue\"; \"it had bitten off many a bait without suffering any damage to its body.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97f50193-1567-4fde-99ec-3403f5af9eed",
                                                "sense_id": "48f6e5b2-c410-3f8b-965e-c18155c5b89e",
                                                "text": "In due course they reached the far side of the Element of Water, gourd annex. The path lead through a translucent vertical wall, and there seemed to be no special challenge to passing through it, except for their fishly status."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f3bdba0-1964-45a8-9c88-ad439ec1d92f",
                                                "sense_id": "48f6e5b2-c410-3f8b-965e-c18155c5b89e",
                                                "text": "\"In sooth, the fellow talks as if in earnest,\" remarked the king, after a moment's reflection, \"and though the request is, perhaps, the strangest to which I have ever listened, I really see no reason why I should not turn a fishly ear.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
